## Quality Assurance Checklist

### Before Committing Tests

- [ ] **Test Coverage**: All new code has corresponding tests
- [ ] **Test Names**: Descriptive test names following conventions
- [ ] **Mock Data**: Proper mocking of external dependencies
- [ ] **Error Cases**: Both success and error scenarios tested
- [ ] **Async Handling**: Proper handling of async operations
- [ ] **Cleanup**: Proper cleanup in `afterEach`/`afterAll`
- [ ] **Performance**: Tests run quickly and don't timeout
- [ ] **CI Compatibility**: Tests pass in CI environment

### Test Review Checklist

- [ ] **Readability**: Tests are easy to understand
- [ ] **Maintainability**: Tests won't break with minor changes
- [ ] **Reliability**: Tests are deterministic and stable
- [ ] **Coverage**: Important code paths are tested
- [ ] **Edge Cases**: Boundary conditions are tested
- [ ] **Integration**: Component interactions are tested
- [ ] **Accessibility**: UI tests include accessibility checks

## Common Testing Anti-Patterns

### ❌ Avoid These Patterns

```javascript
// ❌ Testing implementation details
it('should call setState', () => {
  const component = shallow(<MyComponent />);
  component.instance().setState({ data: 'test' });
  expect(component.state().data).toBe('test');
});

// ❌ Over-mocking
it('should render component', () => {
  jest.mock('../../hooks/useAuth', () => ({
    useAuth: () => ({ user: null, loading: false })
  }));
  // Too many mocks make tests brittle
});

// ❌ Testing multiple things in one test
it('should handle user interaction and API call and error handling', () => {
  // This test is doing too much
});

// ❌ Not cleaning up
it('should set up timers', () => {
  jest.useFakeTimers();
  // Missing jest.useRealTimers() in afterEach
});
```

### ✅ Use These Patterns Instead

```javascript
// ✅ Testing behavior, not implementation
it('should display user data when loaded', () => {
  render(<UserProfile userId="123" />);
  expect(screen.getByText('John Doe')).toBeInTheDocument();
});

// ✅ Minimal mocking
it('should render component', () => {
  render(<MyComponent />);
  expect(screen.getByRole('button')).toBeInTheDocument();
});

// ✅ Focused tests
it('should handle user click', () => {
  render(<MyComponent />);
  fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button'));
  expect(screen.getByText('Clicked')).toBeInTheDocument();
});

// ✅ Proper cleanup
afterEach(() => {
  jest.useRealTimers();
  jest.clearAllMocks();
});
```

